WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:01.899
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:01.899 --> 00:00:06.620
The honey bee is one of the most incredible
creatures on planet Earth.

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:13.629
Each worker bee grafts tirelessly its entire
lifetime to create just 1/12th of a teaspoon

00:00:13.629 --> 00:00:14.999
of honey.

00:00:14.999 --> 00:00:19.340
So when you put honey on your toast in the
morning you are eating the entire lifetime

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:21.750
achievements of around 40 bees.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:28.710
Bees can communicate with each other with
incredible accuracy, via the medium of dance.

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:34.730
Bees have various dances to tell other hive
members where the best, nectar-rich flowers

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:36.050
are located.

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:41.440
Through these waggle dances they can convey
information such as distance, direction, the

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:47.290
angle of the flowers relative to the sun and
even how good the flowers are.

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:51.640
Bee pollination is crucial to the survival
of mankind.

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:57.020
The activities of bees nurtures the crops
we humans live off.

00:00:57.020 --> 00:01:05.019
In fact over one-third of all food you find
in the supermarket requires bee pollination

00:01:05.019 --> 00:01:06.869
to exist.

00:01:06.869 --> 00:01:12.229
If there were no bees, 33% of all foods you
know would be no more.

00:01:12.229 --> 00:01:17.229
And over 90% of the world's plants require
bees.

00:01:17.229 --> 00:01:22.179
Over the past decade there has been an awful
lot of talk about saving the honey bees.

00:01:22.179 --> 00:01:26.899
And you may have heard that the honey bee
has been put onto the endangered species list.

00:01:26.899 --> 00:01:32.540
But this is simply a case of misinformation
being virally spread around the internet as

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:34.409
it often is.

00:01:34.409 --> 00:01:40.679
Truth is, the honey bee is absolutely fine,
there is nothing to worry about.

00:01:40.679 --> 00:01:47.319
In fact, since 2006 the honey bee population
has increased year-on-year.

00:01:47.319 --> 00:01:53.479
It's true that if the honey bee population
drastically decreased it could cause a total

00:01:53.479 --> 00:02:00.249
ecosystem breakdown and the end of the human
race, a terrifying thought.

00:02:00.249 --> 00:02:06.259
But with hundreds of thousands of private
bee keepers worldwide the chances of honey

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:11.099
bees becoming endangered are basically non-existent.

00:02:11.099 --> 00:02:14.230
So what was all the panic about?

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:22.020
The only bees that were identified as endangered
were a tiny handful of obscure bee species

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:25.520
that are endemic to Hawaii.

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:30.560
So unless you happen to live in Hawaii, the
bees you see buzzing around you every day,

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:35.720
happily pollinating plants and making honey
are going absolutely nowhere.

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:42.810
But there is an extremely common animal that
poses an even greater threat to the survival

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:45.440
of mankind than the honey bee.

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:50.659
An animal that is the universal mascot of
the internet.

00:02:50.659 --> 00:02:54.910
The internet's court jester, the cat.

00:02:54.910 --> 00:03:02.170
It may have provided you with countless lols,
and you should be very thankful it has, because

00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:08.480
if the cat were to become extinct it would
likely be the end of the human race.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:14.830
Cats are members of a family of carnivores
called felidae, which includes tigers, cougars

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:15.830
and cheetahs.

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:22.890
And like their distant cousins, cats have
sharp retractable claws, amazingly quick reflexes

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:28.180
and sharp teeth that can effortlessly clamp
into its prey's flesh.

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:34.159
But cats have a predatory asset that their
larger, scarier family members don't.

00:03:34.159 --> 00:03:41.270
A cat has a physics-defying, astonishingly
flexible body.

00:03:41.270 --> 00:03:45.030
They are more agile than big cats such as
tigers.

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:52.230
Statistically cats are one of the best hunters
in the entire animal kingdom.

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:59.439
A study found that tigers were only successful
at catching their prey 5% of the time.

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:06.540
Domestic cats are successful 32% of the time,
which means they are listed as the 6th most

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:10.030
successful hunting animal in the world.

00:04:10.030 --> 00:04:16.160
But over in Africa there is an endemic species
of cat known as the Black-footed cat, which

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:23.000
is even more crazy, this species catches its
prey 60% of the time and they make an average

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:26.160
of 14 kills every night.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:33.380
Making the black-footed cat the 2nd most successful
predator in the animal kingdom, the only animal

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:38.370
more successful is the African wild dog at
number one.

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:44.690
All this means that cats are the world's most
well adapted and best predator for catching

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:46.860
small rodents.

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:52.650
Rats and mice, being so small, cute and defenceless
have been forced to develop extraordinary

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:58.890
reaction times, rapid speeds and agility so
they can evade predators.

00:04:58.890 --> 00:05:05.060
Yet the domestic cat still manages to track
them, and catch them with ease.

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:10.730
The sadistic buggers don't even hunt rodents
for food, it is quite literally a game to

00:05:10.730 --> 00:05:12.190
them.

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:18.790
Experts have actually said that a well-fed
cat catches more rodents than a hungry cat,

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:21.250
because they do it for entertainment.

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:23.740
Wow, cats are evil.

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:29.530
And that is exactly why we need cats for our
survival.

00:05:29.530 --> 00:05:36.240
By hunting and killing rodents and rabbits
cats are doing the world a vital service.

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:43.220
Yes, last time your little Meowly Cyrus bought
you a gruesome present, she was saving the

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:44.220
world.

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:52.560
A study in 1997 found that in Britain alone,
house cats collectively kill over 200 million

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:55.720
specimens of wildlife each year.

00:05:55.720 --> 00:06:01.990
Cats therefore play a vital role in keeping
the rodent and rabbit populations in check,

00:06:01.990 --> 00:06:04.080
all over the world.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:10.160
The phrase "breeding likes rabbits" is no
misnomer, each season a rabbit can give birth

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:16.530
to over a hundred babies and if you think
that's bad, rats are even worse.

00:06:16.530 --> 00:06:23.540
A female rat can mate up to 500 times with
various males over a six hour period.

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:32.430
And a single pair of rats can produce over
2,000 offspring per year.

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:40.300
If left to their own devices, a pairs of rats
can have over half a billion descendants within

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:42.930
just three years.

00:06:42.930 --> 00:06:48.190
But thankfully rats and other invasive rodents
aren't left to their own devices.

00:06:48.190 --> 00:06:53.310
They are constantly on the defensive and their
population numbers are maintained at a healthy

00:06:53.310 --> 00:06:57.740
balanced level by the hard work of cats.

00:06:57.740 --> 00:07:04.210
Cats are one of the few animals on the planet
and most certainly the best, that can actually

00:07:04.210 --> 00:07:08.740
hunt and catch notoriously slippery rodents.

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:15.360
Cats therefore are the best method mother
nature has for preventing rat populations

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:20.200
from exploding exponentially and taking over
the world.

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:26.420
Without cats our world would be overrun by
rats within a year or two.

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:32.350
Trillions upon trillions of rodents and other,
small invasive species would invade every

00:07:32.350 --> 00:07:37.660
home, every business and every square mile
of the planet.

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:42.190
But why would this be so terrible?

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:45.830
Are rats really that dangerous?

00:07:45.830 --> 00:07:47.250
Yes.

00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:52.040
Rats pose two major threats to mankind and
the entire ecosystem.

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:54.910
The first is disease.

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:59.801
Although it's sometimes debated by historians,
it is widely thought that rats were the main

00:07:59.801 --> 00:08:02.090
spreader of the bubonic plague.

00:08:02.090 --> 00:08:05.490
A disease which almost wiped out Europe.

00:08:05.490 --> 00:08:11.250
Whether or not rats were responsible for the
black death, their bacteria spreading abilities

00:08:11.250 --> 00:08:14.110
should not be underestimated.

00:08:14.110 --> 00:08:19.740
Rats spend most of their time hanging out
in sewers, around piles of rubbish, and of

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:21.890
course dead animals.

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:25.160
These are not things one would call hygienic.

00:08:25.160 --> 00:08:32.700
There can be several thousand pathogens on
just a centimetre of a rat's fur, most of

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:34.250
which can be spread to humans.

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:40.719
And they don't have to bite you either, disease
can be transmitted to humans through scratches,

00:08:40.719 --> 00:08:45.970
skin contact and worst of all, their excrement
and urine.

00:08:45.970 --> 00:08:52.300
Rats use urine to communicate, to mark territory
and just because they need to go and they

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:56.760
will urinate absolutely anywhere and everywhere.

00:08:56.760 --> 00:09:01.210
Come into contact with it and you're certain
to fall ill.

00:09:01.210 --> 00:09:04.210
Rats carry some rather horrific diseases.

00:09:04.210 --> 00:09:11.190
Such as Hantavirus Pulmonary Syndrome or HPS,
which can be contracted by just breathing

00:09:11.190 --> 00:09:15.540
the air around where a rat has been.

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:22.420
HPS restricts your breathing and is often
fatal, once the onset of symptoms has occurred

00:09:22.420 --> 00:09:27.810
death can happen in as little as a few hours;
so, that's scary.

00:09:27.810 --> 00:09:35.840
But that's just a fraction of the horrors
rats possess, they also carry Typhus, Salmonella,

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:43.650
Meningitis and Leptospirosis, all of which
can be fatal to humans.

00:09:43.650 --> 00:09:50.390
Thankfully most people very rarely come into
contact with rats, due to our hygienic environments

00:09:50.390 --> 00:09:56.240
and most importantly, the global prevalence
of rat-killing cats.

00:09:56.240 --> 00:10:01.690
Without cats there would be no stopping the
rapid multiplication of rats and the inevitable

00:10:01.690 --> 00:10:05.279
outbreaks of many horrific diseases.

00:10:05.279 --> 00:10:12.370
But believe it or not, disease isn't the worst
thing that would happen if rodents took over

00:10:12.370 --> 00:10:13.950
the world.

00:10:13.950 --> 00:10:16.610
Hunger would be the worst thing.

00:10:16.610 --> 00:10:22.620
Cats have us all fooled, thinking they rely
on their owners for survival.

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:27.440
Here's the brutal truth, your cat doesn't
need you.

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:34.590
Cats, even the laziest of house cats, can
find food for themselves quite easily, if

00:10:34.590 --> 00:10:40.100
they choose to, they only eat the food you
provide for them because it's easier.

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:46.120
In fact when your pet kitty brings you a dead
mouse and leaves it on your doorstep, it's

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:51.650
actually trying to teach you how to hunt,
because it thinks you're a pathetic human

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:55.040
that can't find its own food.

00:10:55.040 --> 00:11:01.300
But it's this very behaviour that has thus
far saved us all from mass-starvation.

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:11.380
You see cats hunt and kill a variety of rodents,
such as mice and rats.

00:11:11.380 --> 00:11:15.690
Rodents just love to eat food staples such
as grain.

00:11:15.690 --> 00:11:19.740
The very grain which we all eat every day.

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:23.940
Farm cats play a vital role in the modern
ecosystem.

00:11:23.940 --> 00:11:29.600
By killing mice and rats that live in and
around storage barns where grain is kept,

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:35.810
they stop all the grain from being consumed
or spoiled by the hungry rodents.

00:11:35.810 --> 00:11:46.460
But rats aren't picky, when they're hungry
they will chow down on just about anything,

00:11:46.460 --> 00:11:54.339
from trash, to animal and human cadavers and
any crop or foodstuff that may be lying around.

00:11:54.339 --> 00:12:00.980
In a post-catolyptic world where rats and
mice are free to multiply by the billions,

00:12:00.980 --> 00:12:07.440
each and every one of our food sources would
be decimated or disease-ridden before it even

00:12:07.440 --> 00:12:08.589
leaves the farm.

00:12:08.589 --> 00:12:13.210
A global famine would be an absolute certainty.

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:20.240
Unfortunately disease and food shortages wouldn't
be the end, the entire ecosystem would also

00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:22.720
collapse due to the domino effect.

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:28.060
Macquarie island is a super remote island
owned by Australia.

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:33.210
Viewing the feral cat population on the island
as somewhat of a nuisance, because they were

00:12:33.210 --> 00:12:38.970
killing the local seabirds, a cat eradication
programme was started.

00:12:38.970 --> 00:12:49.000
And between 1985 and 2000 every single feral
cat on the island was killed.

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:56.510
Within no time at all the local rat and rabbit
populations quadrupled, and they in turn,

00:12:56.510 --> 00:13:02.460
caused massive devastation to the island's
vegetation, depleting all food sources for

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:06.280
the countless other animal species they shared
the island with.

00:13:06.280 --> 00:13:13.700
And the scientists soon found out that rats
love to feed on the eggs of the very seabirds

00:13:13.700 --> 00:13:16.220
which they intended to save.

00:13:16.220 --> 00:13:22.560
The local seabird population declined at an
astonishing rate due to the plentiful rats

00:13:22.560 --> 00:13:25.390
and lack of cats.

00:13:25.390 --> 00:13:31.520
The ecosystem is a very delicate balancing
act and this experiment just goes to show

00:13:31.520 --> 00:13:37.780
that we shouldn't mess with it, because the
tiniest of changes can have enormous, irreparable

00:13:37.780 --> 00:13:40.089
effects.

00:13:40.089 --> 00:13:44.840
Humans have still not formulated an effective
method of pest control for rats.

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:51.700
The array of rat poisons available just flat
out don't work, at least not in the long run.

00:13:51.700 --> 00:13:57.220
Rats are smarter than we give them credit
for and as soon as one of the mischief, yes

00:13:57.220 --> 00:14:03.450
that is what a group of rats is called, dies
from eating rat poison the rest of the mischief

00:14:03.450 --> 00:14:10.710
learns not to trust that food location in
the future; either that or they employ a super-taster

00:14:10.710 --> 00:14:14.650
rat called Remy to check all their food before
consumption.

00:14:14.650 --> 00:14:19.540
In recent years scientists have even found
groups of rats that have developed a natural

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:23.230
immunity to rat poisons.

00:14:23.230 --> 00:14:31.649
Until our artificial rodent deterrents are
developed further, cats remain our only truly

00:14:31.649 --> 00:14:39.000
effective weapon against them, so as long
as we have moggie we should be okay, that

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:44.760
is of course, until rats learn how to weaponise
cucumbers.

00:14:44.760 --> 00:14:56.440
Thanks for watching.

